<title>INDIA: Rail freight hike impact on major India firms - JCBK.</title>
<headline>Rail freight hike impact on major India firms - JCBK.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table, prepared by the research division of brokerage James Capel B&amp;K, shows the impact of Thursday's railway budget on leading Indian firms.</p>
<p>The budget announced a 12 percent freight hike on all commodities barring essential items such as grains, edible oils, kerosene and sugar.</p>
<p>Cement and steel sectors will be affected adversely. The impact of this 12 percent hike in freight charges, on the estimated fully diluted earnings per share (FDEPS) of various companies, is given in the following table:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Company			FDEPS-FY98@   % change</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------</p>
<p>FACT				1.40	 -2.20%</p>
<p>Nestle India		    8.00	 -1.77%</p>
<p>Tisco			    17.30	 -1.56%</p>
